  "post": {
    "caption": "Intuit stock fell about 10.8% on Friday (Reuters, afternoon) after it agreed to sell Mailchimp to Bending Spoons for about $3.68 billion, under a third of the roughly $12 billion it paid in 2021, and cut its fiscal 2027 revenue growth forecast to 8-9% from 9-10%.\nCredit Karma's growth outlook fell to 3-7% from 11-13%, on a day the S&P 500 lost 3.6% and closed in a correction.\n\nThe full why, with charts, lands Sunday for members → link in bio.\n\n#Intuit #INTU #Mailchimp #stockmarket #softwarestocks\n\nSources: Reuters via GV Wire and MarketScreener (Nov 20), TipRanks (Nov 20), InvestorsHub via Yahoo Finance (Nov 20), Invezz via TradingView (Nov 20), Yahoo Finance via AOL (Nov 20), TechCrunch (Nov 20). Not investment advice."
